Linux kernel testing for running on WatchGuard T80 (LS1046A)

to run, deploy to usb drive as described in build-and-deploy.sh, then boot using u-boot script:

```shell
usb start
env set kernel_addr_r 0x80080000
env set fdt_addr_r 0x90000000
env set ramdisk_addr_r 0x94000000
load usb 0:1 ${kernel_addr_r} /boot/linux-mainline-t80/Image
load usb 0:1 ${fdt_addr_r} /boot/linux-mainline-t80/fsl-ls1046a-wgt80.dtb
load usb 0:1 ${ramdisk_addr_r} /boot/initramfs.uImage
env set bootargs console=ttyS0,115200 earlycon=uart8250,mmio,0x21c0500 root=/dev/sdb1 rw rootwait
booti ${kernel_addr_r} ${ramdisk_addr_r} ${fdt_addr_r}
```


NOTE: this is just a test, not a complete solution. 
expect things to miss and not work correctly.


current state:

- [?] generally boots okay, uart console works and boots without crashing
- [X] SATA ssd is detected and can be mounted
- [X] thermal sensors work
- [X] 88E6190 Ethernet Switch working
  * [X] individual ports accessible (DSA)?
  * [ ] both backplane connections utilized?
  * [ ] full GBE?
- [X] I2C working
  * [X] RTC
  * [ ] PoE Controller -> visible, but no driver
  * [X] HW Monitor
  * [X] (2x) TMP175 temperature sensors
- [X] MX25U3235F SPI flash working and readable
- [X] front panel (LEDs, reset button) controllable
  * (via sysfs)
  * (GPIOs 535 (button), 537 (status), 538 (mode), 539 (failover), 540 (attn))
- [ ] PCIe slot working


